WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:14.578
Today was the last day of school before Thanksgiving vacation.

2
00:00:14.579 --> 00:00:17.638
And Nina was already feeling thankful.

3
00:00:17.639 --> 00:00:23.243
Her teacher hadn't given the class any homework!

4
00:00:23.244 --> 00:00:27.463
At Kids Central Izzie was wearing an Indian headdress.

5
00:00:27.464 --> 00:00:30.322
She made it in art class.

6
00:00:30.323 --> 00:00:34.489
"I am thankful that Indians taught us how to eat corn.

7
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:36.603
I love corn."

8
00:00:36.604 --> 00:00:41.679
She bounced around.

9
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:46.266
"Ooh! And I'm thankful for pretty flowers!"

10
00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:50.780
Miss Shelly was carrying two large vases filled with flowers.

11
00:00:50.781 --> 00:00:52.632
"Are those for our activity?"

12
00:00:52.633 --> 00:00:56.171
Nina asked, hoping they were.

13
00:00:56.172 --> 00:00:58.220
Miss Shelly nodded.

14
00:00:58.221 --> 00:01:03.139
"The end of autumn means the end of fresh flowers.

15
00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:07.087
We're going to press these flowers and let them dry.

16
00:01:07.088 --> 00:01:11.285
In a few weeks, they'll be ready to use."

17
00:01:11.286 --> 00:01:15.185
"How will we use them?" Nina asked.

18
00:01:15.186 --> 00:01:20.465
"You can use them to make cards," Miss Shelly said.

19
00:01:20.466 --> 00:01:24.483
"Today I brought some flowers that I pressed last month.

20
00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:28.092
After we press flowers, we'll make thank you cards."

21
00:01:28.093 --> 00:01:33.342
"Thanksgiving thank you cards?" Bobby asked.

22
00:01:33.343 --> 00:01:36.349
"Yes," Miss Shelly answered.

23
00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:40.421
"While we're working, think of someone you'd like to thank.

24
00:01:40.422 --> 00:01:44.605
Right now, choose four flowers you'd like to press."

25
00:01:44.606 --> 00:01:48.727
Nina leaned over the orange, yellow, and red flowers.

26
00:01:48.728 --> 00:01:51.684
Everyone else quickly grabbed theirs.

27
00:01:51.685 --> 00:01:54.457
But the flowers were all so pretty.

28
00:01:54.458 --> 00:01:56.722
It was hard to choose.

29
00:01:56.723 --> 00:01:59.318
"Nina, are you ready?"

30
00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:02.042
Miss Shelly was waiting.

31
00:02:02.043 --> 00:02:07.080
Nina closed her eyes and pulled out four flowers.

32
00:02:07.081 --> 00:02:11.338
Then Miss Shelly started showing them how to press flowers.

33
00:02:11.339 --> 00:02:15.269
"Take one piece of paper and fold it in half.

34
00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:19.380
Open it back up, and arrange your flowers on the inside.

35
00:02:19.381 --> 00:02:22.562
Make sure the flowers don't touch each other.

36
00:02:22.563 --> 00:02:26.471
Then fold it shut again."

37
00:02:26.472 --> 00:02:31.474
"Cute. It's like a little flower book," Nina said.

38
00:02:31.475 --> 00:02:35.228
"Now take one of these giant dictionaries."

39
00:02:35.229 --> 00:02:38.424
Miss Shelly held up a fat dictionary.

40
00:02:38.425 --> 00:02:42.474
"The dictionary will press our flowers for us."

41
00:02:42.475 --> 00:02:45.753
"Turn to the very last page of the dictionary.

42
00:02:45.754 --> 00:02:51.961
We're going to put your little flower book in between the last page and the back cover.

43
00:02:51.962 --> 00:02:57.789
In a few weeks, you'll have beautiful pressed flowers," Miss Shelly said.

44
00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:01.755
Nina followed Miss Shelly's directions exactly.

45
00:03:01.756 --> 00:03:06.035
Nina hoped her flowers would come out pretty.

46
00:03:06.036 --> 00:03:10.135
"Did you decide who you'd like to thank?" Miss Shelly asked.

47
00:03:10.136 --> 00:03:12.935
She opened a red tin box.

48
00:03:12.936 --> 00:03:16.069
She lifted out stacks of cardboard.

49
00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:20.886
Nina saw sheets of pressed flowers between the cardboard.

50
00:03:20.887 --> 00:03:23.974
Miss Shelly gave them blank cards.

51
00:03:23.975 --> 00:03:27.856
"Once you've written your card, brush glue on the front.

52
00:03:27.857 --> 00:03:32.096
Then choose some pressed flowers to gently place on top.

53
00:03:32.097 --> 00:03:35.956
In a few weeks, the flowers you pressed today will be dry.

54
00:03:35.957 --> 00:03:43.832
Then you can make cards like these at home."

55
00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:46.029
Nina looked at Miss Shelly.

56
00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:48.955
"Who is your thank you card for?"

57
00:03:48.956 --> 00:03:51.093
Miss Shelly paused.

58
00:03:51.094 --> 00:03:53.596
"My mother," she said.

59
00:03:53.597 --> 00:03:55.446
"What about you?"

60
00:03:55.447 --> 00:03:58.023
Nina smiled shyly.

61
00:03:58.024 --> 00:04:04.236
"It's a secret," she said.

62
00:04:04.237 --> 00:04:08.220
"Time to go!

63
00:04:08.221 --> 00:04:12.974
Nina, don't forget your card," Miss Shelly called.

64
00:04:12.975 --> 00:04:21.755
"I made it for you," Nina told her teacher. "Bye!"

65
00:04:21.756 --> 00:04:24.696
Miss Shelly opened the card.

66
00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:27.375
It said: "Dear Miss Shelly,

67
00:04:27.376 --> 00:04:32.241
Thank you for 238 days of fun at Kids Central.

68
00:04:32.242 --> 00:04:41.248
Happy Thanksgiving! Love, Nina."

69
00:04:41.249 --> 00:04:58.658
[caption_out@
